      "commit": {
        "author": "\"Zach Aller\" <code@example.com>",
        "date": "2026-10-30T21:05:23-05:00",
        "subject": "ci: report all test results and coverage to Codecov (#2292)",
        "body": "* ci: report all test results and coverage to Codecov\n\nWhen the integration tests failed on main, the UI coverage upload was\nskipped, so Codecov got a partial report for that commit. A failing UI\ntest step also kept the integration tests from running, so they produced\nno JUnit report.\n\n- Run each test step and upload step unless the job was cancelled or\n  Build failed.\n- Write JUnit reports from Vitest and upload them under the ui flag.\n- Write a Ginkgo JUnit report from the e2e suite and upload it from\n  every matrix leg, flagged by Kubernetes version.\n- Give the Go test-results upload explicit files and a flag.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nSigned-off-by: Michael Crenshaw <350466+crenshaw-dev@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* ci: keep Vitest's github-actions reporter alongside junit\n\nSetting reporters replaces Vitest's default list, which in GitHub Actions\nalso includes the github-actions reporter for failure annotations.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nSigned-off-by: Michael Crenshaw <350466+crenshaw-dev@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Michael Crenshaw <350466+crenshaw-dev@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
        "sha": "95e6e144a3cb4357c2cb5c750d0e98851ac15a61",
        "repoUrl": "https://github.com/argoproj-labs/gitops-promoter"
      }
    }
  ]
}
